From 53818a124008c7a11eca9e22b25d1276a283fc87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:43:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): kanban drawer: a retried first read stays
 foreground; a warm-cache re-open still sends its read [daveey]

Follow-up to PR #1959 (review 5889506946, non-blocking points 1-2).

1. Retry of a failed first read went out untagged. userOpenReads marked a kind as read before the request was
   sent, so React Query's retry of a failed first task or log read (the shared queryClient keeps the default
   retry: 3) got {} and the slow-link thinner could skip it as a background poll. userOpenReads now wraps the read:
   a kind keeps priority 'foreground' until one read of it has answered, and only then do its refetches become
   polls.
2. Warm cache. The shared staleTime is 60 s, so re-opening a task whose cached detail/log was <60 s old did no
   mount fetch; the open's first request was the interval refetch 3-30 s later, which then carried the foreground
   tag. PR #1959's "the re-open is sent" did not hold for that case. Both drawer queries now set
   refetchOnMount: 'always', so every open sends its (foreground) read at mount, and the drawer comment says so.
   Cost: one task and one log GET per open of a task opened in the last 60 s.

Tests (fail before, pass after), drawer.test.tsx:
- "keeps a retried first read foreground: a read counts as delivered only once it answered"
  (before: ['foreground', undefined])
- "sends a foreground read when a task is re-opened while its cache is still fresh" (staleTime 60 s client;
  before: no second read)
Kanban plugin vitest 144/144, tsc --noEmit clean, eslint clean on the touched files.
